# Historical cross-method fallback program, now a located negative.
# beta reads shared before its own declaration, and neither caller nor
# beta's lexical parent supplies a visible shared. A future own field is
# not a hidden-input source. The former 0/222 expectation and claim of
# author authority were superseded by the forward/down rule and Q8 U2.
# unit_site_parent_fallback preserves the valid parent-field 0/222 case
# and the unrelated alpha111 contamination control. Executable statements
# below remain unchanged so the obsolete acceptance cannot disappear.
fn: alpha () int
    int: shared 111
    return: 0
end: alpha

fn: beta () int
    c.printf: "beta sees shared=%d\n" shared
    int: shared 222
    return: 0
end: beta

alpha()
beta()
beta()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
